  "readmeFile": "PACKAGE.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.2.0 — Fixes two defaults that made the library unusable out of the box.\nBackendUrl now points at https://verifier-backend.eudiw.dev (the REST API). It previously\ndefaulted to https://verifier.eudiw.dev, which serves the Angular demo UI and answers the API\npaths with 405.\nNew VerifierSettings.IntendedUseId (scalar, default \"TEST-01\") is sent as intended_use_id when a\ntransaction carries none of its own — mirroring how ResponseMode backs ResponseModes. Since August\n2026 eudiw.dev rejects any request without one (MissingRegistrationCertificate); TEST-01 is the\npublic test intended use it publishes at GET /ui/intended-uses. A per-backend IntendedUseIds entry\nstill wins; set IntendedUseId to \"\" when pointing at a backend of your own.\nBoth defaults only apply where nothing is configured, so existing configuration is unaffected.\n\n1.1.0 — Multi-backend support: serve several trust ecosystems from one app.\nAdded VerifierSettings.Backends / DefaultBackend / MdocOnlyBackends / IntendedUseIds /\nResponseModes, the TransactionOptions type, intended_use_id on the init request, and the\nGerman EUDI Wallet (Bundesdruckerei prototype) PID as a further SD-JWT VC option.\nNote: InitializeTransactionAsync gained an optional TransactionOptions parameter ahead of\nthe CancellationToken. Calls passing the token by name or omitting it are unaffected;\npositional InitializeTransactionAsync(ct) calls must be updated to (null, ct).",
